class_name LandmarkWestminsterPlan
extends RefCounted

## Ground plan of the Palace of Westminster in the model frame: origin at
## the Elizabeth Tower's centre, +X across the river front (east, turned
## 6.2 deg from true north by the registry yaw, the palace's own axis),
## +Z along it to the south. Rectangles are fitted to the OpenStreetMap
## building parts of the palace (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors):
## x0, z0, x1, z1 in metres and the wall height. The towers, Westminster
## Hall and the Central Tower are separate masses (SOLIDS) built by
## their own classes; the rest of the palace is the ranges round the
## eleven courtyards.

